Changes in this distribution
----------------------------

This distribution merges five local modifications that previously lived in
two mutually unsynchronized copies (site-packages vs the IDA plugins dir),
and makes the whole thing installable from a wheel:

  - ida_mcp/api_core.py          search_text rewritten: chunked rendering +
                                 in-memory matching with a time budget
  - ida_mcp/sync.py              panic-patch 4/5: no idc.batch() re-entry,
                                 timeout enforced by the waiting thread
  - ida_mcp/api_survey.py        panic-patch 2: refuse survey_binary on
                                 very large databases
  - broker/cache_handlers.py     filter/paging semantics for the cache layer
  - ida_mcp.py                   also unload the broker package on reconnect

Packaging work (original to this distribution):

  - launcher.py                  stdio launcher moved into the package and
                                 de-hardcoded; ida-mcp-launcher command
  - setup_cli.py                 ida-mcp-setup one-shot installer
  - serverInfo.version           read from package metadata, not hardcoded
  - installer.py                 also install/remove the broker/ package
  - packages/dsh-ida-mcp/        the DeepSeek Harness plugin (npm: dsh-ida-mcp)

See PATCHES.md for the reasoning behind each change.


Naming
------

This distribution is published under its own names because the upstream
names are taken:

  PyPI package   ida-pro-mcp-enhanced
                 (ida-pro-mcp on PyPI belongs to mrexodia and stops at 1.4.0;
                  it contains no broker/ and no launcher)
  Python module  ida_pro_mcp_enhanced
                 (deliberately different from upstream's ida_pro_mcp so that
                  installing both packages cannot overwrite each other's files)
  npm package    dsh-ida-mcp

The IDA-side plugin still uses the top-level module names ida_mcp and broker,
because that is how IDA loads plugins from %APPDATA%\Hex-Rays\IDA Pro\plugins.


